  "description": "BAVQAS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H77 Cl7 Dy6 N13 O29 1+,N1 O3 1-,4.5(C1 H4 O1),1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.688-4.087 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.09-117.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(teaH)2(teaH2)2(CO3)(NO3)2(chp)7(H2O)](NO3)·4.5MeOH·1.5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
